# {{.Title}}

A course for [Nabu](https://github.com/mrmxf/nabu).

```bash
nabu seed      # load content/ into pb_data (run from this folder)
nabu serve     # http://127.0.0.1:8090
nabu build     # static site in dist/ (guest lessons work with no server)
```

Content lives in `content/{{.Course}}/`. The full authoring guide is the
[nabu-tutorial](https://github.com/mrmxf/nabu-tutorial) course.
{{- if .Library}}

This course builds its own binary with Nabu as a Go library:

```bash
go get github.com/mrmxf/nabu@latest   # first time: adds Nabu to go.mod
go build -o {{.Binary}} .
./{{.Binary}} seed && ./{{.Binary}} serve
```

The web app is a build output of Nabu, not part of the Go module: put a built
`pb_public/` beside the data dir (see Nabu's README).
{{- end}}
